{"id":"01M4GAK4AVC8C60THTQG2ZCYA7","t":1,"a":"83a1","op":"create","title":"spec: siren-sequence-diagram-slice — Siren core — Sequence Diagram support"}
{"id":"01M4GAK4B5E6ZAEN3D2SJGSG4T","t":2,"a":"83a1","op":"set","k":"description","v":"Legacy: `.scratch/siren-sequence-diagram-slice/`\n\n---\n\n# Siren core — Sequence Diagram support\n\n## Problem\n\n`@siren/core` currently renders exactly one diagram type: `flowchart TD|LR`. Mermaid's own\nsequence diagram is the next most commonly authored diagram type and Siren's whole premise is\nMermaid-syntax alignment, so the parser/graph-model/layout/renderer pipeline needs a second,\nstructurally different diagram type behind it: lane-based, time-ordered, with nested\ncontrol-flow regions — none of which fit `layoutGraph.ts`'s dagre-based rank/position model.\n`SirenDocument` is currently a single monomorphic shape (always flowchart-shaped); this slice is\nthe first time the pipeline needs to represent more than one diagram type at all.\n\n## Outcome\n\nA developer can write a `sequenceDiagram` document — participants/actors, all ten Mermaid message\narrow styles, nested `loop`/`alt`/`else`/`opt`/`par`/`and`/`critical`/`option`/`break`/`rect`\nblocks, `create`/`destroy` participant lifecycle, `box` participant grouping, `title`, and\n`autonumber` — pass it to the existing `render(source, container)` entry point, and see a\ncorrectly laid-out static SVG sequence diagram mounted into the DOM. `render()` still accepts\nflowchart documents exactly as before (regression-safe). Verifiable via automated tests against\neach stage's seam, plus a browser demo page.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `sequenceDiagram` header recognition, dispatched from the same `parseSiren`/`buildGraphModel`\n  public entry points flowchart already uses (`SirenDocument` becomes a `kind`-discriminated\n  union).\n- `participant X` / `participant X as Label` / `actor X` / `actor X as Label` — explicit\n  declarations only, no implicit auto-creation from first message mention. `actor` renders as a\n  stick-figure icon; `participant` renders as a box. Lane order = first-declaration order.\n- All ten Mermaid message arrow styles, modeled as two independent axes: line style\n  (`solid`/`dotted`) × arrowhead (`none`/`filled`/`bidirectionalFilled`/`cross`/`open`) —\n  `->`, `-->`, `->>`, `-->>`, `<<->>`, `<<-->>`, `-x`, `--x`, `-)`, `--)`.\n- Self-messages (`A->>A`).\n- Nested control-flow blocks, recursively: `loop`, `alt`/`else` (any number of `else` branches),\n  `opt`, `par`/`and` (any number of `and` branches), `critical`/`option` (any number of `option`\n  branches), `break`, `rect rgb(...)`/`rect rgba(...)` background highlight. Each block's\n  horizontal extent spans the leftmost-to-rightmost participant lane touched anywhere in its body\n  (recursively through nested blocks).\n- `create participant X` / `create actor X` — lifeline (and its box) starts at that statement's\n  position instead of the diagram's top. `destroy X` — lifeline ends at that statement's position\n  with an X mark instead of reaching the bottom.\n- `box <color>? <label>? ... end` — background-highlighted grouping of adjacent participant\n  declarations.\n- `title <text>` — one line, rendered once at the top of the diagram.\n- `autonumber` / `autonumber off` — toggles sequential numbering of messages (including inside\n  nested blocks) from that point in the document; a bare on/off toggle only.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- `activate`/`deactivate` and the `+`/`-` activation shorthand (activation bars) — deferred.\n- `Note left of`/`Note right of`/`Note over` — deferred.\n- Wiring sequence-diagram participants/messages into the existing `timeline:` step-reveal\n  animation block — deferred. Sequence diagrams render fully visible, static, with\n  `SirenRenderResult.controller` always `null`. If animation is added later it likely needs its\n  own vocabulary (e.g. \"reveal up through message N\") rather than reusing `enter`/`exit`/\n  `highlight` verbatim, since message order is already an inherent property of the diagram —\n  that redesign is out of scope here.\n- `autonumber <start> <step>` custom numbering — only the bare on/off toggle is in scope.\n- `%%` comment lines — not supported by the existing flowchart parser either; a pre-existing gap,\n  not a sequence-specific one.\n- Multi-line / rich-text labels (`<br/>`, Markdown, HTML) anywhere — single-line plain text only,\n  consistent with flowchart node labels.\n- `link` participant links, `actorParticipantPair`, `%%{init}%%` directives, `zenuml` — not\n  discussed, out of scope.\n- Any reuse of `layoutGraph.ts` (dagre) for sequence diagrams — confirmed architecturally\n  incompatible (fixed lane order + nested regions, not a rank/position graph problem); a\n  hand-rolled layout algorithm is in scope instead.\n\n## Domain decisions\n\n- **Sequence document**: a parsed `sequenceDiagram` source — `title`, a flat `participants` list\n  (declaration and `create` statements produce the same participant record, distinguished by\n  where their declaring statement sits in `statements`), a `boxes` list, and a recursive\n  `statements` tree (messages and nested-block statements, in source order).\n- **Statement**: one node in the sequence's recursive body tree. Leaf kinds: `message`,\n  `participant` (covers both `participant X` and `create participant X` — see below),\n  `destroy`, `autonumberOn`, `autonumberOff`. Block kinds (each carrying a nested `body` or\n  `branches` of statement lists): `loop`, `alt` (branches = `if` + N `else`), `opt`, `par`\n  (branches = N `and`), `critical` (branches = `if` + N `option`), `break`, `rect`.\n- **Participant statement**: distinguishes a plain preamble declaration (`participant X` /\n  `actor X`, written before the first message — renders a box/icon at both the top and bottom of\n  its lifeline, unless later `destroy`ed) from a `create` declaration (`create participant X` /\n  `create actor X`, appearing among the statements — renders only at that point, no top box,\n  lifeline starts there). Both produce the same `SequenceParticipantStatement` shape; an\n  `origin: \"declared\" | \"created\"` field carries the distinction the renderer needs.\n- **Explicit-reference rule**: a message, `destroy`, or block referencing a participant id that\n  has no earlier `participant`/`create participant` statement is an error diagnostic (mirrors\n  flowchart's \"no implicit node creation\" stance) — \"earlier\" meaning earlier in the flattened\n  statement order, so a message inside a `loop` can't reference a participant only `create`d\n  later in that same loop body.\n- **Message arrow**: `{ line: \"solid\" | \"dotted\"; head: \"none\" | \"filled\" |\n  \"bidirectionalFilled\" | \"cross\" | \"open\" }`. Two independent axes instead of ten opaque names —\n  matches how Mermaid's own syntax composes them and halves the cases the renderer switches on.\n- **Message id**: auto-generated as `${fromId}-${toId}`, `${fromId}-${toId}#2` for a repeat pair —\n  same convention flowchart edges already use.\n- **Block id**: auto-generated as `${kind}-${n}`, a 1-based counter per block kind in document\n  order (e.g. `loop-1`, `alt-1`, `alt-2`). **Box id**: `box-${n}`.\n- **Lane order**: participants/actors lay out left-to-right in first-declaration order (preamble\n  declarations first in file order, then any `create`-declared participants in the order their\n  `create` statement appears) — `create` does not reorder lanes, it only affects the lifeline's\n  vertical extent.\n- **Block horizontal extent**: a block's bounding box spans from the leftmost to the rightmost\n  participant lane referenced anywhere in its body, computed recursively (a nested block's own\n  extent contributes to its parent's).\n- **SVG conventions** (frozen now so the four pipeline-stage tickets can be built and tested\n  independently):\n  - `<g class=\"siren-participant\" data-siren-id=\"{id}\">` — a `<rect>`+`<text>` for `participant`,\n    a stick-figure `<g>` (head circle + body/arm/leg lines) + `<text>` label for `actor`. Always\n    rendered once at the top of its own lifeline — the diagram's participant row for\n    `origin: \"declared\"`, the `create` statement's row for `origin: \"created\"` — and rendered a\n    second time at the bottom of the diagram only when the participant is `origin: \"declared\"`\n    and never destroyed. So: a plain declared participant gets two boxes, a `create`d one gets\n    one, and a destroyed one gets one plus an X mark.\n    (Clarified after tickets 13/14: the original wording read as though a `create`d participant\n    got only a bottom box, contradicting this spec's own \"Participant statement\" domain\n    decision. Behavior described here is what Mermaid itself does and what ticket 16 implements.)\n  - `<line class=\"siren-lifeline\" data-siren-id=\"{id}\">` — dashed vertical line spanning the\n    participant's computed extent.\n  - `<g class=\"siren-message\" data-siren-id=\"{id}\">` containing a `<path class=\"siren-message-arrow\">`\n    (marker-end/marker-start per arrowhead, `stroke-dasharray` for `dotted`) and a\n    `<text class=\"siren-message-label\">`; an `<text class=\"siren-autonumber\">` is added as a\n    sibling when autonumbering is active for that message.\n  - `<g class=\"siren-block\" data-siren-id=\"{id}\" data-siren-block-kind=\"{kind}\">` — for the six\n    outlined kinds (`loop`/`alt`/`opt`/`par`/`critical`/`break`): a\n    `<rect class=\"siren-block-frame\">`, a `<text class=\"siren-block-label\">` for its header\n    condition text, one `<line class=\"siren-block-divider\">` + `<text class=\"siren-block-label\">`\n    per branch after the first (`else`/`and`/`option`), and nested child elements. A `rect`\n    block instead gets a filled `<rect class=\"siren-block-fill\">` and no frame or labels — a\n    background highlight is not an outlined region, so it does not reuse `siren-block-frame`.\n    (Clarified after ticket 10's review: the original wording named `siren-block-frame` for\n    every kind, including `rect`.)\n  - `<g class=\"siren-box\" data-siren-id=\"{id}\">` — a background `<rect>` (+ `<text>` label if\n    given), rendered before (visually behind) the participants it groups.\n  - `<path class=\"siren-destroy-mark\" data-siren-id=\"{participantId}\">` — an X at the lifeline's\n    truncation point.\n  - `<text class=\"siren-title\">` — once, at the top of the diagram, only when `title` is present.\n  - Label/title/block-condition text is always set via `textContent`, never `innerHTML` — same\n    hard invariant as flowchart.\n\n## Design contract\n\n### `packages/core/src/contracts.ts` (extended)\n\n- Responsibilities: `SirenDocument` becomes `{ kind: \"flowchart\"; ... } | { kind: \"sequence\";\n  ... }`. Adds the full sequence type surface for the entire scope above in one pass — including\n  block/create/destroy/box types even though ticket 01 only implements core parsing — so no later\n  ticket needs to touch this file again and create cross-wave write-ownership collisions.\n  New exports: `SequenceDocument`, `SequenceParticipantDecl`, `SequenceBox`,\n  `SequenceStatement` (recursive union), `SequenceArrowLine`, `SequenceArrowHead`, `SequenceModel`\n  (post-`buildSequenceModel` validated shape — resolved ids, resolved lifeline extents, resolved\n  block participant-touch sets), `PositionedSequenceDiagram`, `PositionedParticipant`,\n  `PositionedMessage`, `PositionedBlock`, `PositionedBox`, `PositionedDestroyMark`.\n- Non-responsibilities: no functions, no logic — types and JSDoc only, same as today.\n- Interface: pure TypeScript type/interface exports.\n- Seam: this file remains the seam that unlocks parallel work across all three waves.\n- Dependencies: none.\n\n### Parser (`packages/core/src/parser/`)\n\n- Responsibilities: `parseSiren(source): ParseResult` sniffs the first non-blank line\n  (`flowchart TD|LR` vs `sequenceDiagram`) and dispatches to `parseFlowchart` (existing logic,\n  extracted verbatim) or `parseSequenceDiagram` (new). `parseSequenceDiagram(source): { document:\n  SequenceDocument | null; diagnostics: Diagnostic[] }` recognizes `sequenceDiagram`, participant/\n  actor/create/destroy statements, all ten message arrow forms, `title`, `autonumber`/`autonumber\n  off`, and — once tickets 06/11 land — the seven block kinds and `box` grouping. Reports syntax\n  diagnostics without throwing, same discipline as the flowchart parser.\n- Non-responsibilities: does not validate that referenced participant ids were actually declared,\n  does not compute lifeline extents or block participant-touch sets (graph-model's job); no\n  layout, no rendering.\n- Interface: `parseSiren(source: string): ParseResult` (unchanged public signature).\n  `parseSequenceDiagram(source: string): ParseResult` (new, independently exported for direct\n  unit testing, same shape).\n- Seam: both functions — string in, data out.\n- Dependencies: none (hand-written parser, same as flowchart).\n\n### Graph model (`packages/core/src/graph-model/`)\n\n- Responsibilities: `buildGraphModel(document): GraphModelResult` dispatches on `document.kind` to\n  `buildFlowchartModel` (existing logic, extracted) or `buildSequenceModel` (new).\n  `buildSequenceModel(document: SequenceDocument): { model: SequenceModel | null; diagnostics:\n  Diagnostic[] }` assigns message/block/box ids, enforces the explicit-reference rule, computes\n  each participant's lifeline extent (`createdAt`/`destroyedAt` position markers), and — once\n  tickets 07/12 land — each block's recursive participant-touch set and each box's member list.\n- Non-responsibilities: no coordinates, no rendering.\n- Interface: `buildGraphModel(document: SirenDocument): GraphModelResult` (unchanged signature).\n  `buildSequenceModel(document: SequenceDocument): { model: SequenceModel | null; diagnostics:\n  Diagnostic[] }` (new).\n- Seam: `buildSequenceModel` itself — testable with hand-built `SequenceDocument` fixtures,\n  independent of the real parser.\n- Dependencies: none.\n\n### Layout (`packages/core/src/layout/`, new file `layoutSequence.ts`)\n\n- Responsibilities: `layoutSequence(model: SequenceModel, options: LayoutOptions):\n  PositionedSequenceDiagram`. Assigns lane x-positions (declaration order), each participant's\n  lifeline y-extent, each message's y-coordinate and label position, and — once tickets 08/13\n  land — each block's recursive bounding box and each box-group's background rect. Hand-rolled\n  top-to-bottom/left-to-right algorithm; does not use `@dagrejs/dagre` (architecturally the wrong\n  tool for fixed-lane, nested-region layout).\n- Non-responsibilities: no SVG, no styling.\n- Interface: `layoutSequence(model: SequenceModel, options: { measureText: TextMeasurer }):\n  PositionedSequenceDiagram`. Reuses the existing `LayoutOptions`/`TextMeasurer` seam unchanged.\n- Seam: the `TextMeasurer` injection point — same fake-in-tests, real-in-browser split as\n  `layoutGraph`.\n- Dependencies: none (no dagre).\n\n### Renderer (`packages/core/src/renderer/`, new file `renderSequenceToSVG.ts`)\n\n- Responsibilities: `renderSequenceToSVG(diagram: PositionedSequenceDiagram): SVGSVGElement`.\n  Builds the SVG tree per the frozen SVG conventions above: participant/actor shapes, lifelines,\n  all ten arrow-marker/dash combinations, message labels, title, autonumber labels, and — once\n  tickets 09/14 land — block frames/dividers/labels and box backgrounds/destroy marks. Emits\n  `data-siren-id` on every element (forward-compatible with a future animation slice, even though\n  none is wired up in this one).\n- Non-responsibilities: does not decide layout, does not attach animation/playback.\n- Interface: `renderSequenceToSVG(diagram: PositionedSequenceDiagram): SVGSVGElement`.\n- Seam: the DOM itself — jsdom in tests, real browser DOM in the demo, same as `renderToSVG`.\n- Dependencies: DOM global only.\n\n### Public API (`packages/core/src/index.ts`)\n\n- Responsibilities: `render()` keeps its exact existing signature. After `parseSiren`/\n  `buildGraphModel`, branches on `document.kind`: `\"flowchart\"` runs the existing\n  `layoutGraph`→`renderToSVG`→`createAnimationController` chain unchanged; `\"sequence\"` runs\n  `layoutSequence`→`renderSequenceToSVG` and returns `controller: null`.\n- Non-responsibilities: no diagram-type auto-detection beyond what `parseSiren` already does.\n- Interface: `render(source: string, container: HTMLElement, options?): SirenRenderResult`\n  (unchanged).\n- Seam: the primary end-to-end integration seam — acceptance criteria for each wave are tested\n  here, mirroring the flowchart slice's own `render()`-level acceptance tests.\n- Dependencies: composes the modules above.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `render()` on a `flowchart TD|LR` document behaves exactly as before this slice (no\n      regression) — existing flowchart test suite passes unmodified.\n- [ ] `render()` on a `sequenceDiagram` document with `participant`/`actor` declarations and one\n      message of each of the ten arrow forms mounts an SVG with one `<g class=\"siren-participant\">`\n      per declared participant (box for `participant`, stick figure for `actor`), one\n      `<line class=\"siren-lifeline\">` per participant, and one `<g class=\"siren-message\">` per\n      message with the correct marker/dash combination for its arrow form.\n- [ ] A message referencing an undeclared participant id produces an error diagnostic; `render()`\n      does not throw.\n- [ ] A `sequenceDiagram` document containing `loop`, `alt`/`else`, `opt`, `par`/`and`,\n      `critical`/`option`, `break`, and `rect` blocks (including nested combinations) renders one\n      `<g class=\"siren-block\">` per block, correctly bounding the participant lanes it touches,\n      with divider lines/labels for every extra branch.\n- [ ] `create participant`/`create actor` produces a lifeline that starts at that statement's\n      vertical position with no top box; `destroy` produces a lifeline that ends at that\n      statement's position with an X mark and no bottom box.\n- [ ] `box <color> <label> ... end` renders one `<g class=\"siren-box\">` background rect behind its\n      member participants.\n- [ ] `title <text>` renders one `<text class=\"siren-title\">`; its absence renders no title\n      element.\n- [ ] `autonumber` assigns sequential `<text class=\"siren-autonumber\">` labels to every following\n      message (including inside nested blocks) in document order; `autonumber off` stops it;\n      messages before the first `autonumber` carry no autonumber label.\n- [ ] `SirenRenderResult.controller` is `null` for every sequence-diagram render.\n- [ ] All label/title/block-condition text is inserted via `textContent` only — content that looks\n      like markup renders as literal visible text.\n- [ ] `demos/sequence-diagram.html`, built against the real `@siren/core` Vite bundle, visibly\n      renders a sequence diagram exercising every feature in scope, opened in a browser.\n\n## Test strategy\n\n- `parseSequenceDiagram` — unit, pure function, no environment. `parseSiren` dispatch — unit,\n  covers both `flowchart` and `sequenceDiagram` headers routing correctly.\n- `buildSequenceModel` — unit, pure function, hand-built `SequenceDocument` fixtures.\n- `layoutSequence` — unit, pure function, fake deterministic `TextMeasurer` (same fake as\n  `layoutGraph`'s tests).\n- `renderSequenceToSVG` — component test under Vitest's jsdom environment, hand-built\n  `PositionedSequenceDiagram` fixtures.\n- `render()` — integration test under jsdom, exercising the acceptance criteria above; the demo\n  page is verified manually in a real browser (automated browser e2e remains out of scope, same\n  as the flowchart slice).\n\n## Verification\n\n- Focused: `pnpm --filter @siren/core test -- <file>`\n- Suite: `pnpm --filter @siren/core test`\n- Static: `pnpm --filter @siren/core exec tsc --noEmit`\n\n## Baseline\n\nMeasured 2026-09-04 on `main` (`a14ac3e`): `pnpm --filter @siren/core test` — 6 test files, 65\ntests, all passing. `pnpm --filter @siren/core exec tsc --noEmit` — 0 errors. Clean baseline; any\nfailure surfacing during this slice is new.\n\n## Risks and deferred questions\n\n- **Ticket count / total scope**: this board covers nearly the full Mermaid sequence-diagram\n  grammar (everything except activation bars, notes, and animation integration) in one pass\n  rather than split across multiple slices — a deliberate choice made with the user, trading a\n  larger board for not having to re-open planning later. 15 tickets, in three waves (core →\n  control-flow blocks → create/destroy/box), each wave landing a real, demoable capability.\n- **Parallelism is real but wave-bound**: within a wave, the four pipeline-stage tickets\n  (parser/graph-model/layout/renderer) are genuinely file-disjoint and safely parallel once their\n  wave's blocking ticket(s) land. Across waves, the parser/graph-model/layout/renderer tickets\n  each extend the *same file* the previous wave's ticket created, so they are correctly serial\n  within their own lane (e.g. ticket 06 blocked-by ticket 01, ticket 11 blocked-by ticket 06) —\n  this is an honest file-collision constraint, not under-parallelized planning.\n- **contracts.ts frozen for the whole board up front**: ticket 01 must get the full type shape\n  right for all three waves, not just core parsing. If a later wave's implementation reveals the\n  frozen shape is wrong (e.g. block participant-touch sets need a different representation), the\n  fix fans across every ticket that already built against it — same interface-first risk the\n  original flowchart slice's spec flagged, recorded here rather than hidden.\n- **`autonumber off` scope**: included as a bare toggle; custom start/step numbers\n  (`autonumber 10 5`) explicitly excluded — flagged in Non-goals for visibility since it wasn't a\n  separately asked question.\n- **Block condition/branch label text**: assumed single-line plain text (`loop Every minute`,\n  `alt is sick`), consistent with the \"no rich text anywhere\" non-goal — not separately asked."}
